.TH BINGUX-WEATHER 1 "2026-11-09" "Bingux 0.1.0" "Bingux"
.SH NAME
bingux-weather \- forecasts for the Bingux desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bingux-weather
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bingux-weather
opens the Weather window: the conditions now, the next 24 hours, ten days, the
UV index, wind, sunrise and sunset, the moon, humidity, pressure, visibility and
the air quality, for the computer's position and for the cities that were added.
.PP
Only one Weather window runs.
A second launch raises the running window.
.PP
The forecast, the air quality and the city search are Open-Meteo's
(https://open-meteo.com), licensed CC BY 4.0, and need no key.
.SH POSITION
"My Location" is found with the desktop's location service
(the Location portal) when there is one, and otherwise from the network
address, which is accurate to about the city.
The window says which.
Turn "Use my location" off in the menu to use only the cities that were added.
.SH UNITS
Units follow the locale (\fBLC_ALL\fR, \fBLC_MEASUREMENT\fR, then \fBLANG\fR)
until they are chosen under Units in the menu.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+R, F5
Refresh.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
Add a location.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy the conditions.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Page Down, Ctrl+Page Up
Next and previous place.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BINGUX_WEATHER_DIR
Keep the settings and the cached forecasts under this folder (\fIconfig/\fR and
\fIcache/\fR) instead of the XDG folders.
.TP
.B HTTPS_PROXY
The proxy the requests go through.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bingux/weather/settings.json
The saved places, the units and the place on show.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bingux/weather/here.json
Where the computer was last found.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/bingux/weather/forecast-*.json
The last forecast of each place, shown with its age when there is no network.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bingux\-settings (1)
.PP
Documentation: docs/weather.md in the Bingux source.
